# .gitattributes of the looping-agent fixture, ORI-T-0076.
#
# This directory becomes a repository of its own when a test copies it and runs
# git over the copy (make-repo.sh). That repository does not inherit the
# attributes of the Ori Studio repository it is committed inside, so it carries
# its own. Without them a Windows machine whose git has core.autocrlf=true
# writes CRLF into every worktree of the copy, and a shell script whose first
# line ends in a carriage return does not run as written, so agent.sh would fail
# on its own line endings instead of failing the way it is built to.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
